%rec: Archive
%doc: Entry point of a smart-archive disc: which format and version this is, which disc,
+ and where its other catalogue files are (paths relative to the disc root).
+ Specification: tools/arv/docs/spec/smart-archive-format.md
%mandatory: Format Version Disc Uuid

Format: smart-archive
Version: 0.5
Disc: FAM-02_2019_Y
Uuid: UUID
HomeUuid: UUID
Manifest: manifest-sha256.txt
Listing: catalog/volumes/FAM-02_2019_Y/listing.tsv
Snapshot: catalog/archive.rec
Viewer: index.html
Payload: data/

%rec: Disc
%doc: One record per physical disc image (an OAIS AIP). Field names follow
+ Dublin Core terms where one fits: Title, Creator, Date, Description,
+ Subject, Coverage, Rights. Uuid is the machine identity of the image
+ (copies burned from one image share it); Id is for people and is
+ derived from Set, Sequence and Coverage (EDTF) under IdScheme, so it
+ can always be regenerated and checked (see docs/spec/smart-archive-format.md).
%key: Id
%mandatory: Id Title Date
%type: Uuid uuid
%type: Sequence int
%type: Date date
%type: Files int
%type: Bytes int
%type: Access enum public private sealed
%type: Retired date

Id: FAM-02_2019_Y
Uuid: UUID
IdScheme: set-seq-coverage/1
Label: FAM-02_2019_Y Family photos
Title: Family photos
Collection: FAM
Set: CODE
Path: PROJECTS/CODE
Sequence: 2
Coverage: 2019
Date: 2026-01-01
Creator: archivist
Access: public
Files: 2
Bytes: 4
Software: SW

%rec: Binding
%doc: How one volume is stored on its medium: the container (filesystem) and the
+ protection (error correction) it was made with. These change with the medium;
+ the files and the rest of the catalogue do not (research/plan.md, four layers).
+ Container: iso9660+udf-1.02, udf-2.50 (later perhaps ltfs, exfat, tar, afs).
+ Protection: rs03 or none. Media, Filesystem and Ecc describe them for people
+ (format 0.2 and earlier kept those three in the Disc record).
%key: Volume
%mandatory: Volume Container Protection
%type: MediumSectors int

Volume: FAM-02_2019_Y
Container: udf-2.50
Protection: none
Media: M-DISC BD-R 25GB
Filesystem: UDF 2.50, BD-ROM layout with metadata partition and a real mirror (arv udfwrite)
Ecc: none

%rec: Collection
%doc: Something kept over time and made into discs again and again, e.g. a family's
+ photos: one workflow folder, one history of Revision records. Uuid is its identity
+ (it survives renames, moves and changes; the folder's .arv marker carries it); Code
+ is for people and prefixes its disc ids. Title, Description, Set, Category and
+ Access are the defaults its discs are made with.
%key: Code
%mandatory: Code Uuid Title
%type: Uuid uuid
%type: Access enum public private sealed

Code: FAM
Uuid: UUID
Title: Family photos
Set: CODE
Access: public

%rec: Revision
%doc: One state of a collection, as git's commits are: appended, never edited. Tree is
+ the SHA-256 of its manifest (every file's path and SHA-256, sorted); Node is the
+ SHA-256 of Tree, Parent(s), Date and Message, and names the revision. A checkpoint
+ only records the state (the files stay on everyday storage); an edition became discs:
+ Edition numbers it, Volume names each disc. Each edition is a full copy of the
+ collection, with as many copies as its owner makes (discs, NAS); a later safe edition
+ replaces earlier ones, except those with Keep: yes (which may be added later: it is
+ not part of Node).
%key: Node
%mandatory: Node Collection Tree Date Stage
%type: Date date
%type: Edition int
%type: Stage enum checkpoint edition
%type: Keep enum yes

Node: 95a366ff6ab057524819f4269e38c7d31178aefdd18888fdd07fc629a4554183
Collection: UUID
Tree: c4092301849c111763072e3a030ef3dc4d1f4c4ced1a7929ca5145b9115ab718
Parent: 1436106577dc489c0d805d34f07fce5c8af9e3fed51904b8c7e368f5ebc1cd7d
Date: 2026-01-01
Stage: edition
Edition: 2
Volume: FAM-02_2019_Y
Changes: +1 ~1 -1 >0 files
Message: the 2019 sort

%rec: Event
%doc: Preservation actions and metadata changes, appended and never edited. Type uses
+ the PREMIS eventType vocabulary: https://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/preservation/eventType
+ Disc names the disc; a change to a location or a selection names it in Object
+ (location:CODE, selection:CODE) instead.
+ Agent (one or more) is software (arv@COMMIT), a model (llm:MODEL, embeddings:MODEL) or a person (human:LOGIN).
+ Authorship says how people and machines shared the work: automatic (software
+ following rules), suggested (a model, not reviewed), accepted (a model's suggestion
+ a person kept as it was), edited (one a person changed), human (a person alone).
+ A replication with ReadBack: identical is a copy read back against its image before it
+ was recorded (known good); deaccession retires a disc (its Disc record gets Retired).
%mandatory: Type Date Outcome
%type: Outcome enum success failure warning
%type: Authorship enum automatic suggested accepted edited human

Disc: FAM-02_2019_Y
Type: message digest calculation
Date: 2026-01-01
Outcome: success
Authorship: automatic
Agent: SW
Note: sha256 and sha512 manifests of 2 files
